{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>ו אִישׁ</b> ('each man') — by way of analogy." "<b>גִּבּוֹר</b> — the male species, and because he mentioned כַּגִּבּוֹרִים יְרוּצוֹן ('they run like warriors')." "<b>וּבְעַד הַשֶּׁלַח</b> — a weapon of war, like מֵעֲבוֹר בְּשֶׁלַח ('from wielding a weapon'), and there is no sending-away in war." "<b>לֹא יִבְצְעוּ</b> — like וְלֹא יִפְצְעוּ ('they do not break ranks'), and similar: וּבָצְעָם בְּרֹאשׁ כֻּלָּם ('and their breach at the head of them all')."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {3 "The comparison of לא יבצעו to ולא יפצעו follows a well-known rabbinic tradition (Targum, Rashi) treating the root בצע here as equivalent to פצע; the second comparison, ובצעם בראש כולם, is cited from an unclear source and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:35.292631691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}